course: dictionary
lesson: 14621
title: Signs of things to come
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Portend is a formal word. It means to be a sign or warning that something important is going to happen, and that thing is often bad. «Dark clouds portend a storm.» The clouds are not the storm yet. They are a sign that a storm is coming.
explain: Portend can also mean to point to something in the future. Look for two clues: a sign, and something that is still to come. If you find both, portend probably fits. Test it by swapping in «warns of». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Portend is a stiff, bookish word, so you will meet it mostly in stories, old tales and formal writing. In everyday talk, people say «suggest» or «show» instead. Portend has a stronger feel: it hints at something big and important coming.
fact: Portend is a verb, so its forms are portend, portends, portended and portending.
fact: «Portend» means to be a sign or warning that something important, often bad, is going to happen.
fact: With he, she or it, use portends: «The strange silence portends trouble.»
fact: Common phrases include «portend trouble», «portend disaster» and «portend change».
fact: Portend is formal, so in everyday writing use words like suggest, show or warn.
exercise: «Dark clouds portend a storm.» What does portend mean here? | * Are a sign that a storm is coming | Are very dark and pretty | Stop the rain from falling | Hide the sun behind them
exercise: «The strange silence portends disaster.» What is the best swap for portends? | Forgets | * Warns of | Ends | Hides
exercise: Ella says portend means to paint. What does it really mean? | To count money carefully | * To be a sign that something important is coming | To paint a picture | To run very fast
test: «The dark cloud portended trouble.» Which word is closest in meaning to portended? | * Warned of | Slept under | Rained on | Danced with
test: The flashing red light portends a crash. What does this tell you? | The crash has already stopped | The car has been fixed and is safe | It is only a bright colour with no meaning | * It shows a crash is likely to come
exam: «The bright comet portends great change.» What does portends mean? | Is a sad story about a comet | * Is a sign that great change is coming | Is a bright light that has no meaning | Ends the change before it starts
